1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Warrant answers questions about US federal employment regulation.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,500
It answers as of a date — because the law changes, and the
right answer changes with it.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Here is one question asked as it stood in 2020.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
9,438 paragraphs were eligible. Sixteen came back, each one
cited to a specific paragraph of the regulation.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,500
The stamped ones are superseded. About half of this corpus is
text that no longer applies.

6
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:35,500
Now the same question, at a later date.

7
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:42,000
Different evidence, different answer — and both are correct,
on their own dates.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
"The service period may not exceed 4 years."
Grounded in a specific version of a specific paragraph.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Now a follow-up — and notice it is pinned to the same date.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
A normal chatbot would have to guess which year you meant.
Guess wrong and it quotes repealed law with confidence.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
So this endpoint has no date parameter at all. There is no way
to send a different one.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Every stage recorded what it saw and what it cost — so a wrong
answer has an address, not an excuse.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Code, and every measurement including the negative ones:
github.com/tasnimuldatascience/warrant
